# AX88179B (0b95:1790) — see ~/projects/ax88179/PLAN.md
#
# 1. Force USB config 1 (vendor-specific) so a real Ethernet driver binds. The dongle boots in
#    config 2 (CDC-NCM), where cdc_ncm claims it as a dumb pipe with no PHY control.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="0b95", ATTR{idProduct}=="1790", ATTR{bConfigurationValue}!="1", ATTR{bConfigurationValue}="1"

# 2. Disable USB autosuspend — aggressive autosuspend re-enumerated the dongle every ~4s.
#    ORDER MATTERS: this must come AFTER the bConfigurationValue line above. Setting the
#    config re-inits the device and resets power/control, so the original rule (which set
#    power/control first) silently lost this write.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="0b95", ATTR{idProduct}=="1790", ATTR{power/control}="on"
